      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Ports are rows with rules",
        "statement": "Each port is a row: id, direction, side and offset, data type, which edge classes it accepts, and what dragging from it creates. The node class and the edge class then meet at the port, and each side states its half of the rule.",
        "status": "spark",
        "confidence": "unproven",
        "notes": "Edge classes state which kinds they connect. Ports already carry allowed edge types (the Event Handler and Method ports accept only invokes). A node template would be where those are authored instead of scattered in code.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
